cs/adr/0007-review-bot-receiver.md is unrelated and must not be edited'"],"finding":"The plan body cites `docs/adr/0007-jira-onboard-config-write.md` as an edit target, but ADR 0007 is actually `0007-review-bot-receiver.md` (unrelated) and the jira-onboard ADR is `0070-jira-onboard-config-write.md`. The body path is misnumbered/hallucinated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f137df835e0b8b62d","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan body, 'Enumerated consumers — jira-onboard -> bridge setup' Docs line; reconciled in 'Binding review remediation > Correct ADR and consumer inventory'","norm_id":"n02e6a73ec11aa9ce","priority":0.5312,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An implementer following the plan body rather than the remediation section edits the wrong ADR or opens a non-existent path"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Update the body 'Docs' line under the jira-onboard consumer set to cite `docs/adr/0070-jira-onboard-config-write.md`, matching the binding-review remediation.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the dispatch/registration shape for `bridge fsck` and `bridge check-access` as explicitly as `bridge setup`: state that they attach as bridge-group children whose `bridge_cli` arms route to `bridge_fsck.main` and the `_bridge_probe` launcher respectively (NOT `launch_reconciler`), and update the required-subparser metavar and group help accordingly.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current `_bridge_commands.py:_parser()` registers only preview/sync/pause/resume with `required=True` subparsers and metavar `{preview,sync,pause,resume}`, and `bridge_cli` forwards every parsed command to `launch_reconciler` / `_pause_or_resume`.","`bridge-fsck` today routes via `_cli/__init__.py:_dispatch_bridge` to `bridge_fsck.main(rest)` (NOT the reconciler); `bridge-probe`/check-access routes via the `_bridge_probe` subprocess launcher (`__init__.py:165`). Neither goes through `launch_reconciler`.","The plan gives an explicit dispatch contract for `setup` (add_help=False + argparse.REMAINDER delegating to jira_onboard) but no equivalent statement for how `fsck` and `check-access` become children of the bridge group without being mis-wired through the reconciler or breaking the required-subparser/metavar."],"finding":"The plan specifies the pass-through argparse shape for `bridge setup` in detail but leaves the dispatch/registration shape for `bridge fsck` and `bridge check-access` implicit, even though neither routes through the reconciler that the existing `bridge` argparse group forwards to.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2b136c092684398","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Binding review remediation -> `bridge setup` dispatch shape; Enumerated consumers (bridge-fsck / bridge-probe)","norm_id":"n6c4d049123ea24d9","priority":0.4169,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Implementer adds `fsck`/`check-access` as bridge subparsers but leaves `b